# Copy this file to `.env` for local Expo runs. Never commit a real `.env`
# (it is gitignored). Do not paste keys into chat or GitHub.
#
# Windows: the file must be named exactly `.env` (not `.env.txt`).
# Notepad often appends .txt — Save As with name ".env" in quotes, or turn on
# "File name extensions" in Explorer and rename. Then restart:
#   npx expo start -c
# Installable build (preferred; not Expo Go):
#   npx expo start --dev-client

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (preferred phone path — cloud only, like LightLift)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With these two set, signup / login / homes / ledger / safety recalls talk to
# Supabase directly. No laptop API and no EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL / LAN IP required.
# Recalls need epic7 SQL: ../../supabase/migrations/20261120000000_epic7_recalls.sql
#
# Dev/test tip: Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Email → Confirm email → OFF
# so sign-up returns a session immediately (no inbox wait).
#
# Option A — Expo public names (typical local .env):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_KEY

# Option B — Cursor / Cloud secrets (EXPO_PUBLIC_ names are reserved in
# Cursor bind-app-secrets). app.config.js maps these onto Expo public names.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_KEY

# Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in the phone app.
# Schema + founder steps: ../../supabase/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI assist (SERVER ONLY — LightLift pattern)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER put GEMINI_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / AI_API_KEY in this Expo app or
# any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable. The phone calls Supabase edge function
# `ai-assist`, which reads the key from Edge Function secrets.
#
# Set on the Supabase project (Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets, or CLI):
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-key          # preferred — same name as LightLift
#   # OPENAI_API_KEY=...                    # alternate
#   # AI_API_KEY=...                        # alternate
# Optional:
#   GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
#   AI_ASSIST_LIVE=true
#
# Deploy: supabase functions deploy ai-assist
# See ../../supabase/functions/ai-assist/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android push (FCM) — EAS builds only; not a Metro .env value
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lock-screen push on Android needs google-services.json baked into the APK.
# Do NOT put the Firebase service-account private key here.
#
# Preferred: upload google-services.json as EAS file env GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON
# with visibility **sensitive** (not secret) for development / preview /
# production. app.config.js maps it to android.googleServicesFile and EAS
# Android builds fail if it is missing. Then rebuild the preview APK.
#
# Alternate: place apps/mobile/google-services.json (gitignored) for local
# prebuild. Cloud builds still need the EAS file env unless you force-add.
#
# Steps: README.md → Android lock-screen push (FCM)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HomeAsset API (optional — local SQLite demo OR hosted cron / jobs)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed when Supabase URL + anon are set (cloud signup/login + AI).
# Simulator / same PC without Supabase: leave unset (defaults to localhost:8787).
# Physical phone on the SQLite demo path only — use your PC LAN IPv4:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787
#
# Windows — find the IP: Command Prompt → ipconfig → IPv4 under Wi‑Fi / Ethernet.
